      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not 100% sure where to put this comment, since it relates to several spread out areas.\n\nI\u0027m wondering if it\u0027s possible to leverage this new Uniform type more, to simplify the processor index and uniform index iteration patterns, the emitCode generation and the uniform writing.\n\nSpecifically, once setUniforms() is called, the Uniform index within the GrProcessor is constant. But we have to refer back to these indices when we call GrUniformWriter::write(...) and when we findUniform(). If we could somehow pass the Uniform into these functions instead, I wonder if it would read nicer (e.g. writer.writeSkMatrix(p, kViewMatrix, ...)) and avoid needing to do map lookups from the aggregator? A findUniform() update would be aggregator.getMangledUniform(p, kViewMatrix)\n\nI have not tried actually writing code, but just imagining ways to remove magic indices from the calling code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 150,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 150,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "1cca14705e996bbeee6f779e10bfdbc252e55d28",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
